      'Turn-flow example: 1. Setup: prepare players, deck or tiles, and opening layout according to the variant. 2. Turn loop: each player performs one legal action (play, capture, build, bet, or pass/draw as applicable). 3. Resolution: each action updates control of tricks/cards/pot/layout. 4. End condition: when hand-ending criteria are met, scoring is computed and match state advances.',
      'Scoring example: Teams track progress on a five-rung score comb, erasing one rung for each point earned by winning a hand, winning all nine tricks, or scoring from legal risks and smacks with the King of hearts. The first partnership to erase all five rungs on their side of the score comb wins the game; the number of remaining rungs on the losing side shows the margin of victory..',
